.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_CONCAT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_concat ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_concatenate
.Nd merge the contents of streams
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely_ops.h
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_concat "dtfl_stream *a" "dtfl_stream *b"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_stream_concatenate "dtfl_scope *scope" "dtfl_stream *const *streams" "size_t n"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_stream_concat
produces a stream carrying every record of both
.Fa a
and
.Fa b ,
each at its original time.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_concatenate
is the general form: it merges the
.Fa n
streams in
.Fa streams ,
all built in
.Fa scope ,
into a single output stream.
.Fn dtfl_stream_concat
is
.Fn dtfl_stream_concatenate
over the two given streams.
.Pp
Every source must carry the same record type, which becomes the output
stream's type.
The operator does not reorder or retime records; it only unites the
streams.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Both functions return the merged stream, owned by the scope.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_stream *merged = dtfl_stream_concat(left, right);

dtfl_stream *parts[3] = { s0, s1, s2 };
dtfl_stream *all = dtfl_stream_concatenate(scope, parts, 3);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes.
Mixing record types across the sources is a programming error and calls
the panic hook.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_stream_count 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_exchange 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_map 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_partition 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_to_stream 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Fn concat
and
.Fn concatenate
operators.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The operator and its streams belong to the worker thread that built
them and must not be shared.
